<main id="content" class="site-main post mt-article"><div class="page-header"><h1 class="entry-title">Top Indoor Water Features to Add to Your Spa</h1></div><div class="page-content"><p class="mt-article-meta"><time datetime="2024-04-05T21:26:00">April 5, 2024</time></p><div class="mt-article-body">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A spa is a place that everyone visits to escape their busy life and to have some peace while getting pampered. As a spa owner, your goal should be to turn your space into as serene as possible ?and what better way to do so than to use some fantastic water features in it? There isn&#8217;t.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, to help you choose the best water feature, we bring you the top four designs that turn your place into a calm heaven.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">1. Wall-Mounted Waterfalls:</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wall-mounted&nbsp;<strong><a href="/">waterfall walls indoor&nbsp;</a></strong>are a beautiful focal point that adds both visual appeal and auditory delight to your spa. Since the spa is all about calmness and peace, these water features offer precisely that. You can also customize these features according to the look of your place. Imagine a gentle stream of water cascading down a stone or glass wall, creating a sense of relaxation. The gentle sound and water flow can create a calming and welcoming environment in the space, which everyone wants in a spa.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">2. Zen-Inspired Water Fountains:</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For a truly tranquil spa experience, consider adding a Zen-inspired water fountain into your space. These fountains are usually placed outdoors, but since we are talking about spas, they can be placed indoors, too. Whether it&#8217;s a simple tabletop Zen fountain or a larger floor-standing model, the gentle trickle of water from the setting adds a sense of movement and life to your spa environment. You can create a corner or a center point in the waiting area inside your spa to bring tranquility to the place.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">3. Indoor Pond or Water Garden:</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bring the beauty of nature indoors with an indoor pond or water garden. Like <strong><a href="/bubble-walls/">water walls</a></strong>, these huge water features create a little escape point inside the spa, complete with lush greenery, floating lilies, and perhaps even a few koi fish gliding gracefully beneath the surface. Imagine customers sipping coffee in your spa and gazing at this beautiful scenery that you built inside your place, feeling a sense of connection to the natural world. These aren&#8217;t just to make your spa look pretty but also to bring a calmness and peaceful effect to the place and everyone who visits.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">4. Bubble Walls:&nbsp;</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Consider installing a bubble&nbsp;<strong><a href="/waterwalls/">water curtain wall&nbsp;</a></strong>in your spa for a modern and playful twist on traditional water features. Having such a mesmerizing display means that your customers won&#8217;t get bored if they have to wait for their turn because they will keep gazing at the bubbles that bobble on the bubble wall. Whether used as a standalone feature or along with other water features, bubble walls are a sure way to excite everyone.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, what do you prefer? The tranquil simplicity of an indoor water wall, the Zen-inspired tabletop fountain, the natural beauty of an indoor pond, or the modern playfulness of a bubble wall? Whichever you like there&#8217;s a water feature design to suit every style and preference. So why wait? Choose your design from these top 4 indoor water features and bring life to your spa.</p>
</div></div></main>

